Z||000002||fropuff||09-08-2000||04:57 PM||||What a piece of crap that writer is!  He obviously doesn't know anything about Fieros, like Sushi said.  He said that crap about the suspension and handling, then about how crappy they were, period.  That stupid bastard doesn't know what he's talking about.  He said that it's not a sports car, which it's not.  He compared it to the 'Vette and Porsche.  What an idiot!  Let's compare:  1980s Fiero: about a $5000 maximum, which is for the top-of-the-line Fiero.  1980s 'Vette:  about $20,000. 1980s Porsche: about $20,000.  I'm not sure of the exact prices; I might be way off.  I was just comparing.  What does this mean?  Well, it's a 4:1 ratio.  4 Fieros for every 1 Corvette or Porsche.  This guy is a piece of work.  My brother subscribes to all the car magazines; I'll have to look at it and e-mail them.  ||||reg||1
