Z||000005||2xsess||09-08-2000||05:40 PM||||Someone please give me the email address for those asses!!! I never thought that their mag was worth a s**t anyways. MY 88GT held the road with my fathers 88 'vette, so much so that he used to ask me to trade him for days at a time!!! That author doesn't realize how many of us there are out here who still love that little car!!! And he obviously didn't do his homework! <p>[This message has been edited by 2xsess (edited 09-08-2000).]||||reg||8
Z||000006||Raydar||09-08-2000||05:56 PM||||Yeah? Well screw 'em.<BR>Automobile magazine has never been a serious automotive journalistic effort, anyway.<BR>It mainly consists of writers who left Car & Driver, and several of the other car mags. It seems to pride itself on ignoring logical thought processes (and hard performance numbers), and looking down its nose with disdain at what it perceives to be "great unwashed" of automobiledom. <BR>Pretty pictures on glossy paper, and not much else. <BR>Just consider the source.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<BR>88 Formula T-Top <BR>88 Coupe (ISO big V-6)<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||13
Z||000007||mshill||09-08-2000||06:25 PM||||Someone sure got his panties in a bunch.  I wonder who pissed him off.  Just the fact that he sights Yahoo as a source of information demonstrates this guy doesn't know how to do research.  All in all the article had little if any tangible facts and at best was a subjective personal opinion.<P>The only redeeming thing about the article was the very nice Red GT pictured above it.  With a car that looks that good I think I would have to drive it before I passed judgement.||||reg||1
Z||000008||Monkeyman||09-08-2000||06:32 PM||||fropuff--About 15 grand for an '88 GT, but I get your point.  I think the ratio of Fieros:Vettes was probably more like 1:2.5 but you're close enough. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000009||gixxer||09-08-2000||06:34 PM||||Ahahahaha! I guess that's the sort of writing you could expect from people who write about 1957 DeSotos, and go into dreary detail about changes of tail fin height and optional fake spinner hub caps. <BR>In many cases they never open the hood of the car they're reviewing...probably can't find the latch. <BR>Automo-bile Magazine is only a downscale "Robbe Report" anyway...(or is it the other way around), so I wouldn't get too upset about an article written by second string writers.<BR>Just my opinion, of course. ||||reg||1
Z||000010||Fformula88||09-08-2000||10:01 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"><P>OK!  We now have 1300+ members on this forum.  LETS FORM A MOB AND HUNT THAT WRITER DOWN!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif">  Not only doesn't he know much about the Fiero, he doesn't know much about GM either.  He says they didn't ressurect the plant due to there being :no residual value in the concept".  I take this to mean the plastic body on frame construction from the context.  Somebody please introduce him the the Pontiac Trans Sports between 1990-1996.  Ok, so they were built in Terrytown NY, but they were still using the same technology.  Sorry to rant on about it... but its just a brainless attempt to sell a magazine by exploiting the popularly held view of the Fiero being a major dissappointment and failure.  Cancel that mag!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/Motorcity/Boulevard/9278/fierosig1.jpg">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||8
Z||000011||Homicidal||09-09-2000||12:36 AM||||Guys guys GUYS!  I am PLENTY mad, just as much as you are.  But this writer is the epitomy of what is wrong with the attitude toward the Fiero.  This is what people actually think of our little plastic beauties, and while it's great to rant and rave about his <I>opinion</I>, we won't change anything.  The Fiero is known as a low-quality car among the <I>un-educated</I> people.  <P>Come on guys, what do we care what some idiot writer of a car magazine says?  We KNOW everything he said was 100% false, and I for one do not care if he DOES think that way, his loss.  He'll be eating those words eventually, trust me.  I mean, he obviously ignores the OBVIOUS, he stated there were more clubs than GTO and Firebird combined.  Does that sound like a car that has sub-sedan quality handeling?  Sure it does........  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>Many writers said the Mustang was one of the worst production cars and would NEVER be a classic, EVER.  Yup, that sure held up.<P>Let's not let out maturity run away from us, we know that guy is inept on the Fiero facts.  Let's just enjoy our cars, and we can flip him off when we scream by his MR2!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by Homicidal (edited 09-09-2000).]||||reg||11
Z||000012||Oreif||09-09-2000||12:52 AM||||What a lame article! If the guy even remotely knew what he was talking about he'd be dangerous. Well Guess what It's time to straighten them out!<BR>Look what I found!<P>feedback@automobilemag.com<P>Yes it is their Email. Let's correct this fabricated story!<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-09-2000).]||||reg||8
Z||000013||Oreif||09-09-2000||01:10 AM||||I just sent them an Email expressing my "Views" of their writer.<BR>I was polite and tactfully and pointed out that if the writer could find a station wagon that could out handle a Fiero, I'd prove them wrong on an enclosed road course.<BR>Also mentioned that the writer should actually drive the vehicle he is commenting on.<P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-09-2000).]||||reg||4
Z||000014||Oreif||09-09-2000||09:25 AM||||No response yet to my Email yet, But I'm waiting.||||reg||13
Z||000015||Greg Piet||09-09-2000||12:08 PM||||OK I too sent an e mail.....<BR>Here it is<P>I have recently read an article in your "Views" section regarding the Pontiac Fiero.  It <BR>seems apparent that the author is not truly familiar with the Pontiac Fiero.  The reason <BR>being is that although there is a strong Fiero owner base to this day who are dedicated <BR>to keeping Pontiacs slogan of "We Build Excitement" true to this day.  One excellent <BR>support base would be Pennocks Fiero Forum out of Holland <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl" TARGET=_blank>www.fiero.nl</A> <P>I was very surprised reading that the Toyota Mr-2 had many traits of a sports car that <BR>the Fiero lacked.  My reason for being so surprised by this statement is from direct <BR>experience.  I am currently a member of the Sports Car Club of America.  In this <BR>organization there are regional events called autocrosses where people race their cars <BR>against the clock and then compare times.  Obviously by me writing this article I am <BR>driving a Pontiac Fiero, which is completely stock.  In my car class I compete against <BR>Toyota Mr-2's, Mazda Miatas, and Mazda Rx-7's to name a few.  This has been my <BR>first season racing in these events, and I am currently in FIRST place against such cars <BR>that have the "performance attributes" that the Fiero is supposedly lacking.<P>There is another thing to consider when comparing the Fiero to such automobiles as <BR>the Corvette.  The primary consideration would be to consider if GM would allow <BR>production of a car that cost less and outperformed its flagship sports car?  If I am not <BR>mistaken (although in this case I might be as I do not have the numbers in front of <BR>me at this time)the V6 Fiero performance stats in 1985 were comparable to the 1985 <BR>corvette barring top speed.<P>Thank you very much for your time,<P>Gregory C Piet ||||reg||1
Z||000016||Fformula88||09-09-2000||12:27 PM||||GREAT!!!  Thanks for their email Orief!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">  I couldn't pass up the opportunity to tell them about their article!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  In a very diplomatic way, I had to show them what a bunch of lies and half truths their article is!<P>I can see the matchup now!  Orief in his Fiero vs.  Automobile Magazine in a 1985 Pontiac 6000 Station Wagon thru a handling course!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Better watch out!  Everyone knows that 6000 pulls .95g on the skidpad  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"><P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.geocities.com/Motorcity/Boulevard/9278/fierosig1.jpg">  <BR>1988 Fiero Formula||||reg||6
Z||000017||Oreif||09-09-2000||12:36 PM||||I have sent them 2 Emails. The first was my opinion of the article, (and the challenge) The second was the TRUE performace facts of fiero's. I got these from another Fiero website where the webmaster used various Road and Track, Car and Driver and Motor Trend magazines to get the averages of performance data aquired by the different magazines.					<BR>  Statistics:					<BR>           1985 Fiero V-6    -    1988 MR2 Supercharged     - 1987 MR2<BR>     					<BR>Size:					<BR>Height:    46.9 inches -          48.6 -inches                48.6 inches	<BR>Width:     68.9 inches   -        65.6 -inches                65.6 inches	<BR>Length:    164.9 inches     -     155.5 inches              - 155.5 inches<BR>Wheelbase: 93.4 inches       -    91.3 inches              -  91.3 inches<BR>Weight:    2712 pounds     -      2780 pounds              -  2389 pounds<BR>					<BR>Tires:     215/60-R14    -        185/60-R14              -   185/60-R14   	<BR>					<BR>Brakes:    9.7-inch front    -    9.6-inch front          -  10.2-inch front<BR>           9.7-inch rear     -    9.4-inch rear           -  10.3-inch rear	<BR>					<BR>Engine:    2.8L MPFI V-6     -   1.6L DOHC 4-cyl with      - 1.6L DOHC 4-cyl<BR>                      -------------------OHV                     supercharger		<BR>					<BR>bhp @ rpm:   140 @ 5200      -        145 @ 6400            -   112 @ 6600<BR>					<BR>torque @					<BR>rpm:         170 @ 3600       -       140 @ 4000             -  97 @ 4800	<BR>					<BR>Compression				<BR>ratio:        8.9:1   -                  8.0:1                 -  9.4:1		<BR>					<BR>					<BR>Performance:				<BR>					<BR>Braking 60-0: 147 feet            -    157 feet              -  150 feet	<BR>					<BR>Skidpad:      .84g          -           .80g             -       .80g	<BR>					<BR>Slalom:       63.9 mph        -        64.0 mph             -   62.5 mph	<BR>					<BR>Time to Distance:				<BR>					<BR>0-30:          2.2  -                     2.1                 -    2.8		<BR>0-60:          7.4   -                    7.5                  -   9.5		<BR>1/4-mile:     15.6 @ 89 mph    -         15.7 @ 87 mph    -    16.9 @ 83 mph<BR>					<BR>Top speed:    128 mph          -       129 mph               -  119 mph	<BR>(best estimates)<P><BR>*				<BR>		                        1/4-mile   +/-  .4 of a second	<BR>		<BR>-  '87 Pontiac Fiero SE       (15.6)		<BR>		<BR>-  '97 Ford Mustang GT              (15.3)	<BR>-  '94 Ford Mustang Cobra           (15.3)	<BR>-  '94 Lexus LS400                  (15.6)		<BR>-  '94 Honda Prelude V-TEC          (15.4)	<BR>-  '96 Honda Del Sol V-TEC          (15.6)	<BR>-  '93 BMW 750 iL                   (15.9)		<BR>-  '94 Acura Integra GS-R           (15.8)	<BR>-  '88 Pontiac Firebird Trans Am    (15.4)	<BR>-  '96 BMW Z3                       (16.1)		<BR>-  '91 Toyota MR2 Turbo             (15.4)	<BR>-  '88 Toyota MR2 Supercharged      (15.4)	<BR>		<BR>		<BR>                        Slalom    +/-  .5 mph 		<BR>        Fiero (63.9 mph)  (note all vehicles listed are slower)<BR>		<BR>-  '92 Dodge Viper               (62.7 mph)	<BR>-  '93 Ferrari 348               (62.8 mph)		<BR>-  '93 Porsche 968               (63.3 mph)	<BR>-  '89 Porsche Carerra 4         (63.3 mph)	<BR>-  '95 BMW M3                    (62.8 mph)	<BR>-  '97 BMW Z3 2.8                (61.4 mph)	<BR>-  '94 Nissan 300ZX Twin Turbo   (63.0 mph)	<BR>-  '94 Mitsubishi Eclipse GSX    (63.6 mph)	<BR>-  '94 Mitsubishi 3000 GT VR-4   (63.7 mph)	<BR>-  '93 Acura NSX                 (62.3 mph)	<BR>-  '94 Chevrolet Corvette        (62.6 mph)	<BR>		<BR>		<BR>                         Skidpad   +/-  .3g		<BR>        Fiero (.84g stock on original tires, .86g on more modern rubber)<BR>		<BR>		<BR>-  '94 Ford Mustang GT            (.86g) 	<BR>-  '95 Lamborghini Diablo VT      (.87g)	<BR>-  '93 Lotus Esprit Turbo         (.86g)		<BR>-  '94 Mitsubishi 3000 GT VR-4    (.86g)	<BR>-  '94 Mitsubishi Eclipse GSX     (.86g)	<BR>-  '93 Acura NSX                  (.87g)		<BR>-  '95 BMW M3                     (.87g)		<BR>-  '97 BMW Z3 2.8                 (.87g)		<BR>-  '96 BMW 740i                   (.82g)		<BR>-  '95 Porsche Carerra 4          (.85g)		<BR>-  '97 Mercedes SLK230 Kompressor (.83g)	<BR>-  '95 Pontiac Firebird Formula   (.85g)	<BR>-  '88 Toyota MR2 Supercharged    (.80g)  ok so it's .1 too low, but hey<BR>		<BR>			<P>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-09-2000).]<p>[This message has been edited by Oreif (edited 09-09-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000018||Philphine||09-10-2000||12:03 AM||||i still think we should try to find the most open minded car mag (scc or maybe even car craft if enough v8 guys wrote), write to them en masse and try to influence them to consider fieros and fiero performance. if they know there's a niche, small though it may be in the over all scheam of things, they might be willing to fill it. if there's 1300 members now and a good percentage of us wrote it ought to get somebodies attention. <p>[This message has been edited by Philphine (edited 09-10-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000019||My7Fieros||09-10-2000||03:48 AM||||In the words of Eric Cartmen (SouthPark)..."This guy is a donkey raping s**t eater!||||reg||1
Z||000020||Cliff Pennock||09-10-2000||05:30 AM||||Well, I have send them an email too:<P><I>Dear sirs,<P>Someone at my online Fiero Forum (http://www.fiero.nl/forum) pointed me to your article about the Pontiac Fiero. Of course, any negative article about a car will generate defensive responses from those who own that very same car. Nobody will ever admit the car they drive really isn't all that good. In this case however, I feel the Fiero is done tremendous injustice and I suspect the author has been led more by hear-say than actual experience.<P>Unfortunately, the Fiero *does* have a bad name, mainly fueled by articles like this one. However, anyone that ever gets to drive one quickly understands there really is no ground for this bad reputation. The Fiero is often referred to as "the poor man's Ferrari" - suggesting that the single reason people are liking them, is the fact that they are cheap. Well, I live in the Netherlands, and Fieros are anything but cheap here. For the price I paid for my Fiero, I could have easily bought myself a used Porsche 911 (which *are* relatively cheap in Europe). The reason I bought my Fiero is for all the reasons your articles states the Fiero lacks. I've driven (and owned) a lot of sportscars, from Corvettes to Porsches and still my favorite is the Fiero. I could now go on and fill pages with reasons why, but I guess that seeing is believing, or in this case "driving is believing".<P>My Fiero Forum has well over 1300 members and I'm sure there are several in your neighborhood who would gladly show you the "real" Fiero. If you are interested in actually taking one for a spin, just let me know. I can arrange this in no time for sure.<P>Sincerely,<P>Clifford Pennock</I>||||reg||1
Z||000021||Fformula88||09-10-2000||10:09 AM||||Nice letter Cliff!  I hope they do take you up on your offer to get behind the wheel of a Fiero!||||reg||1
Z||000022||Monkeyman||09-10-2000||11:31 AM||||I just emailed them, too.  I think I ended my email with "Good luck in the future.  With articles like this, you'll need it.".  I hope they took that as sarcasm (the good luck part).  I hope everyone else noted (in their email) that even though this was in the "Views" column (meaning, I assume, that it's an opinion) it was written as a factual article and came across that way.  Nothing more than childish bashing.  (I hope the writer gets his doors blown off by a Fiero while driving home in his station wagon.)||||reg||1
Z||000023||Jonathan||09-10-2000||08:34 PM||||Often a subject like this comes up that makes us react emotionally, and without clarity of thought.  So without emotion, and a very clear mind, I have this message for the author of this article:  Screw you!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||12
Z||000024||Monkeyman||09-10-2000||09:24 PM||||Well said. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000025||HugGRRRFiero||09-10-2000||11:21 PM||||Man... I'd like to take this guy for one ride in my (GM sedan, station wagon) Fiero.  Just want to see the look on his pale face when I make a sharp left hand turn and he sees the heater core fly thru the passenger door.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>"...a nerd's car."  That's the first I ever heard the econo Fiero's mentioned as a nerd's car.  I'm going to wrap some tape around the bridge of my glasses, pull my pants up high, talk in a squeeky voice, and wear pocket protectors from now on, Get real!!!  <P>Just because a car is a sports car doesn't mean it has to be expensive.  The Fiero was intended to be an affordable, cool looking commuter, which improved it's performance, handling, and looks each year it was produced.  Maybe this guy should log off yahoo.com and get back to the real world.<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/huggrrr.gif">  <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com">HugGRRRFiero@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||8
Z||000026||Cheever2||09-10-2000||11:30 PM||||Seems to me that anybody who has a Fiero wants another (then another, etc).  I don't know anybody yet who couldn't wait to get rid of theirs.  We all know how many out there are pretty rough, but the owners I've met still love to drive 'em.<P>Fiero owners are all smiles; [almost] all other cars are just piles.<BR>||||reg||8
Z||000027||286SE'S||09-11-2000||12:11 PM||||How come no one appreciates articles like this one for the simple reason that it reinforces the general publics' idea that Fieros are no good and that lets us buy them for $300 (with a simple fixable problem). We should only hate the writer if you in the resale business and from reading this Forum, there are some. I see the same cars for sale for weeks in the papers, prices slowly dropping as they realize there are very few buyers.<BR>I always considered the Fieros appeal to be "my special secret". Something that everyone hates but gives me so much pleasure to own and drive. I have never been a "part of the crowd" person.<BR>It is strange that the writer sums the car up as "not very good" with no facts. The pile of second-hand info is pretty typical for this type of magazine. We should be glad that he did not mention the "fires" I  have seen 4 times the amount of burned Chrysler LeBarons than Fieros.<BR>Terry<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000028||stsmithgt||09-11-2000||02:34 PM||||I used to have a muscle car untill I wrapped it around a light pole.  I wish it could have handled as well as this "piece of junk that can't out perform a station wagon".  I Used to have a RX-3 wagon which handled pretty well and would out perform several cars with the rotory engine, but it can't touch this GT even with it's struts in the front.  My GT just saved me from ending up in an orchard the other day.  Almost any other vehicle I've owned would have been wrapped around an almond tree right now.  I don't know how it made it around that curve (that I didn't see coming), but I'm glad it did.  ||||reg||14
Z||000029||btoth||09-11-2000||10:32 PM||||i just recieved my copy of the mag in the mail today... that guy reminded me of all the morons i run into that say "fiero's suck, they catch on fire...", when really they know nothing about the car at all.  i hope to see some of your emails in the Letters section of that mag next month.||||reg||8
Z||000030||RobertVol||09-12-2000||12:25 AM||||Man you guys were real professional in your response..hmm <P>I dont know if its because its Florida / Tenn football weekend next weekend or what but I had to a be a little more to the the point. here ya go : <P>*A beautiful car that will never rust. <P>*Kids come up to me and say WOW!!! I like your car! especially the t tops!<P>*3.8 GEN II SC V-6  5 speed<P>*Handles like a vette and and looks like a ferrari <P>*With all mods on my mint 88GT T top fastback 3.8 SC.....Total ....................$13,500.00 <P>*Times I have had fun in this car.................PRICELESS !!!!!!<P>ISN'T THAT WHAT BEING A CAR ENTHUSIAST IS ALL ABOUT !?!?!?<P>nuff said! <P>PS... 0-60-5.5sec / 1/4-13.6sec  AND NO RELIABILITY PROBLEMS AT ALL<P>Get off the narrow minded track or lose a customer! <P>IN PARTING .....<BR>Oh hey MAN get your miata out of my f__king tailpipe and while your at it that piece of crap overated rice burning MR II covertable thing out also.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <P>Thank you for your cooperation!!!<P>Robert Porter<BR>North Florida Fieros<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> at least I said Thanks you  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000031||Fformula88||09-12-2000||05:37 PM||||I went out and got myself a copy of the mag today.  I decided I had to have a hard copy of this article in my hands.  Anyone who has read Master Sushi's link to the article needs to get a hold of the whole thing to really appreciate it.   <P>I may get some flames for this, but after seeing the whole thing I rather liked it.  Not for what it says, but for the simple fact that Mr. David E. Davis Jr felt it so necessary to write an article about a car now 13 model years removed from production in a mag primarily about new stuff!  In an odd sort of way, this editorial is a compliment to the Fiero.  He even gives all the good points about the car, but doesn't say they are good.  He just needs to really look at what he wrote and he will see our side.<P>I bet he hates Fieros because of the one that was spun out in Manhatten.  He must have been driving it!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||6
Z||000032||DJRice||09-14-2000||09:50 AM||||"Screw that guy, Im going home"<P>Whatever....He needs to wake up and smell what he's shoveling.<P>------------------<BR>Dillon<BR>Black '87 SE V6<BR>"You mean like the back seat of a Volkswagen?"||||reg||1
Z||000033||AkursedX||09-14-2000||10:02 AM||||The only thing that I liked about the article is that it showed an exact picture of my Fiero!!! (Minus the spoiler)   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000034||ur2biteme||09-15-2000||07:12 AM||||ever wonder what happens when birth control only works halfway?  <P>case in point, the intelect of the person who wrote this article.  lets see, higher crash test ratings than volvo all 5 years, faster 0-60 and 1/4 mile than the same year 'vette by .1 second every year of the v6, handles with TODAY'S exotics.  wtf?  you can tell that he did NO research WHATSOEVER.  i bet this guy wears a backwards hat after work when he gets in his riced out civic!  moron. <P>anyway &lt;small world theme&gt;  i guess there's another Robert Porter on the list.  hey, i'll trade you cars.  we wouldn't even need to change titles over......<P>------------------<BR>UR2BITEME<BR>'87 econo coupe<BR>169k and a bad fender :(||||reg||1
